WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.806
Tester: Hi, I'm the tester.

2
00:00:01.806 --> 00:00:07.075
Tester: I'll use VoiceOver, the screen reader built into the Mac, and tell you what I hear.

3
00:00:07.476 --> 00:00:08.796
Reviewer: And I'm the reviewer.

4
00:00:08.796 --> 00:00:13.387
Reviewer: When something sounds wrong, I'll name the WCAG criterion it falls under,

5
00:00:13.387 --> 00:00:17.601
Reviewer: say why it matters, and explain what changed in the code to fix it.

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.654
Reviewer: This video is about WCAG 1.1.1, Non-text Content.

7
00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.785
Reviewer: Anything shown as a picture, like a chart,

8
00:00:24.785 --> 00:00:30.675
Reviewer: needs a text alternative that gives a listener what the picture gives a viewer.

9
00:00:31.077 --> 00:00:34.634
Tester: Here's a quarterly report, in Safari, with VoiceOver on.

10
00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:39.588
Tester: Under the heading there's a bar chart of sales for July, August and September.

11
00:00:39.588 --> 00:00:43.653
Tester: I'll read the page one item at a time, from the link at the top.

12
00:00:47.811 --> 00:00:50.347
VoiceOver: heading level 1 Quarterly report

13
00:00:50.347 --> 00:00:52.970
VoiceOver: How sales went from July to September.

14
00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.544
VoiceOver: q3-sales.svg image

15
00:00:55.544 --> 00:00:57.303
VoiceOver: end of main

16
00:00:57.303 --> 00:01:02.917
Tester: After the sentence under the heading, VoiceOver said q three sales dot S V G, image.

17
00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:06.728
Tester: That's the file name. It never said what the chart shows.

18
00:01:07.128 --> 00:01:09.450
Reviewer: That's a problem under WCAG 1.1.1.

19
00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:14.639
Reviewer: The chart has no text alternative, so VoiceOver falls back to its file name.

20
00:01:14.639 --> 00:01:17.916
Reviewer: If you're listening, you know there's a picture,

21
00:01:17.916 --> 00:01:20.579
Reviewer: but not that sales went up every month.

22
00:01:23.179 --> 00:01:25.696
Reviewer: In the code, the image now has alt text.

23
00:01:25.696 --> 00:01:29.851
Reviewer: It says it's a bar chart, what it measures, and the three numbers.

24
00:01:29.851 --> 00:01:31.929
Reviewer: The chart looks exactly the same.

25
00:01:32.332 --> 00:01:35.032
Tester: The same reading pass, on the fixed page.

26
00:01:38.923 --> 00:01:41.475
VoiceOver: heading level 1 Quarterly report

27
00:01:41.475 --> 00:01:44.134
VoiceOver: How sales went from July to September.

28
00:01:44.134 --> 00:01:49.906
VoiceOver: Bar chart of sales in the third quarter, in thousands of dollars: July 120, August 150, September 180. image

29
00:01:49.906 --> 00:01:51.641
VoiceOver: end of main

30
00:01:51.641 --> 00:01:55.264
Tester: Now VoiceOver reads the chart: what kind of chart it is,

31
00:01:55.264 --> 00:01:57.141
Tester: and the sales for each month.

32
00:01:57.543 --> 00:02:02.393
Reviewer: A listener gets what the chart shows. 1.1.1 holds here.
